description:
src/lib/budget.ts — pre-flight reserve + post-flight finalize.

  export async function reserveBudget(args: {
    userId: string;
    tier: 'free' | 'pro';
    estimatedCostUsd: number;
  }): Promise<{ allowed: boolean; queries_used: number; usd_used: number; query_limit: number | null; usd_limit: number | null; reason?: 'queries' | 'usd' }>;

  export async function finalizeBudget(args: {
    userId: string;
    estimatedCostUsd: number;
    actualCostUsd: number;
  }): Promise<void>;

reserveBudget:
  - Lazy period reset: if reset_at < now(), zero counters and bump reset_at first.
  - Atomic UPDATE-RETURNING that increments both queries_used (+1) and usd_used (+estimated).
  - Reject if either axis would exceed its (non-null) limit; revert the increment in that case (or use a CTE that only commits if both checks pass).

finalizeBudget:
  - Adjusts usd_used by (actual - estimated), usually negative.

Tier → limits mapping (replaces today's LIMITS const):
  free: { query_limit: 10, usd_limit: null }
  pro:  { query_limit: 30, usd_limit: null }   // future: switch to usd_limit=$0.50/day, query_limit=null

Tests:
- both axes under limit → allowed
- queries_used + 1 == query_limit → allowed (boundary)
- queries_used + 1 > query_limit → rejected with reason='queries'
- usd_used + estimated > usd_limit → rejected with reason='usd'
- query_limit=null → no query enforcement
- usd_limit=null → no usd enforcement
- finalize where actual < estimated → usd_used decreases
- finalize where actual > estimated → usd_used increases (caller probably already passed reserve, this just logs the overage)
- lazy reset: row with stale reset_at returns zeroed counters

Done when:
- reserveBudget + finalizeBudget exported with the signatures above
- tests cover boundary + reject + reset cases
- existing checkAndIncrement is removed (or marked @deprecated and unused after child 5)
